<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Logistics &amp; Transport Accounting?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Specialized financial management of GTAs, fleet operators, warehouses, and freight forwarders: GTA GST under RCM or forward charge, e-way bill documentation, fleet depreciation, consignment-wise revenue, and multi-state GST management. For <a href="/gst-returns">GST Returns</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>For Gurugram logistics &ndash; 50-truck fleet from Bilaspur, 3PL warehouse in Manesar, freight forwarder in Udyog Vihar &ndash; every service must be classified under GTA (SAC 9965), e-way bills generated for every dispatch &gt; Rs 50K, and vehicle-wise revenue/costs tracked. For <a href="#">Import Export Code</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Logistics &amp; Transport Accounting:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>GTA:</strong> Goods Transport Agency issuing consignment notes &ndash; GST under RCM or forward charge</li>
                        <li><strong>E-Way Bill:</strong> Mandatory for goods &gt; Rs 50,000 &ndash; 200 km/day validity &ndash; 200% penalty</li>
                        <li><strong>S44AE:</strong> Presumptive for &le;10 vehicles &ndash; Rs 1,000/ton/month or Rs 7,500/month</li>
                        <li><strong>RCM:</strong> Registered recipient pays 5% GST on behalf of GTA</li>
                        <li><strong>Forward Charge:</strong> GTA opts at FY start &ndash; 5% (no ITC) or 12% (with ITC)</li>
                        <li><strong>SAC 9965:</strong> Goods transport including loading, unloading, packing by GTA</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="column-image">
                <div class="illustration-placeholder">
